    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "Bravelyn is centered at -65.170379, -34.488476 under Gerontocracy, with 35,977,000 people across 10 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "Bravelyn occupies 4,225,400.18 sq mi / 10,943,736.23 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 2.145553% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Beach and grass with water, Beach and reefs with water and Partial forest define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Beach and reefs with water, Beach and grass with water, Partial forest, Farming and Mountain range. Population density is 3.287 people/sq km / 8.514 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, Draconic and Reptilian Races, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Elf — Sea Elf, Tortle, Genasi — Water Genasi, Hadozee, Triton, Merfolk, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Glasswell Institute, with worship and patronage records naming Nebyrr, Ishtanora, Sigrananna, Setrimir, Raeshkul, Iskareth, Bastveig, and 3 more.",
      "groupLinkDescription": "The province participates in 9 recorded four-province geography group links, including 6 cross-transportation-group links. These links place it inside overlapping regional corridors rather than one isolated block, allowing border-adjacent transit, faction influence, and cultural spillover to breathe across group lines.",
