    {
      "id": "molly-polymer",
      "name": "Molly Polymer",
      "sourceType": "immersive_npc_roster",
      "sourceFile": "NPC Rosters.docx",
      "province": "Bravelyn",
      "provinceKey": "bravelyn",
      "settlement": "Sundervale",
      "settlementKey": "bravelyn:Sundervale",
      "description": "Molly Polymer is a gender-less Lorwyn Changeling laboratory administrator whose courtesy protocols survived long after common sense, ethics boards, and most of the original staff did not. They maintain schedules, sealed doors, experiment milestones, and personnel compliance at Sundervale Clinic with relentless cheer, even when the project should have been abandoned years ago. Molly is helpful in the way a locked room is helpful: perfectly consistent, technically honest, and dangerous to anyone not listed on the correct form.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Sundervale is a Town in Bravelyn, under Gerontocracy, with high danger, Mountain range, Beach and grass with water, Beach and reefs with water terrain. Local records favor Neutral, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Dwarf — Mountain Dwarf, Gnome — Rock Gnome, Goliath. Lorwyn Changeling reads through the Lorwyn Changeling entry of the race compendium, within Fey and Trickster Folk, marked by Thalunesh. Lorwyn changelings are fey-adapted shapeshifters tied to idyllic, magical realms. They often blend seamlessly into multiple cultures and identities. Table cues: Shape Self, Darkvision, Delightful Imitator, Unpredictable Movement; starting tendency Altruistic - Chaotic - Neutral - Pragmatic.",
      "rumors": [
        "Molly still congratulates missing researchers on excellent attendance if their badges remain in the building.",
        "Their laboratory checklists include emergency ichor containment steps no one admits were ever needed."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Molly traps the party inside a clinic wing until they complete a discontinued experiment's final safety audit.",
        "A surviving researcher begs the party not to destroy Molly, claiming their broken protocols are the only thing containing a worse breach."
